label a0523:
    # --- Day 9: 2025-05-23 --
    scene bg kitchen
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_home zorder 3 
    with dissolve_scene_full
    play music dailyleisure
    window auto
    "Friday morning arrives with unusual restraint."
    "There are no shenanigans aside from the fact that the smell of charred cinder permeates the kitchen."
    "Somebody doesn't have toast today because they turned the knob on the toaster in the complete other direction."
    "{i}Sucks to be you, Asa~{/i}"
    show mom neut at t22
    show asahina neut at t21
    "My sister sits across from me with one knee tucked against the chair, eating with enough vendetta that it could make an onion cry."
    "Mom has already dressed for work, but she hasn't left yet. That alone makes the morning feel almost ceremonial."
    mom "Track again today, right?"
    mc "Yeah. Light cardio, probably. Or maybe the stupid parachute thingy."
    mc "Coach said Friday depends on whether the foot starts yelling."
    ah "Does it know its rights?"
    "Mom looks over her case folder without changing expression."
    mom "It can retain counsel after breakfast, now finish eating."
    "Asahina lowers her eyes back to her plate, the facetious comment flying over her head."
    "The joke fades instead of breeding more jokes, which is how I know all three of us are still tired from the week."
    "{i}God, I sound like an old man when I say that...{/i}"
    "For a minute, breakfast is only breakfast."
    "Normal sounds, doing normal work, hammering home the fact that they are very normal."
    "The apple juice is particularly pungent--probably a telltale sign of either expiration or the heat death of my tastebuds."
    mom "Oh, [player], before I forget..."
    "{i}There it is.{/i}"
    "The exact tone adults use when they choose the most survivable moment to bring something stress-inducing up."
    mc "...Should I be worried?"
    mom "Not that I know of, unless you have something to tell me."
    mom "I just want to put it back in your brain."
    "{i}That's arguably worse.{/i}"
    mom "The school I mentioned last week."
    mom "I know I said you could come to me when you wanted to dig into it, and I meant that."
    mom "Consider this one practical reminder before midterms eat the calendar."
    mom "If you have the bandwidth tonight, I'd like us to sit down and actually look at it together."
    "She glares at me above her glasses."
    mom "But again, no rush at all."
    "My hand pauses around my cup."
    "The topic of college has a way of making the table feel bigger."
    mc "...Tonight?"
    mom "Yeah, just after dinner and everything. Nothing intense."
    mom "Just the program page, admissions requirements, costs, commute and housing, that kind of thing."
    mom "We're absolutely not deciding your whole life in one evening, rest assured."
    ah "That'd be kinda efficient, though."
    "Her voice is softer than the words."
    "Mom's gaze flicks to her, then back to me."
    mom "Efficiency isn't always kind, you know."
    "The room holds that for a second."
    mc "...Yeah, okay. Tonight works. I got nothing going on."
    mom "Perfect!"
    mom "Bring your laptop down when you're done showering after practice. That way we're not hogging the same screen."
    mc "Whoopty doo."
    "Asahina makes the tiny nose-sound she makes when she almost laughs and decides not to spend the energy."
    "Eventually, the kettle clicks off."
    "Mom closes her folder and stands, and just like that the future gets put into a work bag for later."
    show mom at thide
    hide mom
    show asahina at thide
    hide asahina
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "The rest of the morning behaves."
    nier "Mom leaves with an actual goodbye instead of a sticky note. Asahina remembers her lunch without being chased. I double check my bag, my alarm, and my sock situation with the caution of someone recently humbled."
    nier "Friday does indeed have the decency to start in order."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0523_1
    scene bg class_day
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3 
    stop music fadeout 1.0
    with dissolve_scene_full
    play music quiz
    "Classes move with the expected particular impatience of a few days before exams."
    "Every teacher seems to be offended with the repeat questions of concepts covered a month ago and whether or not this or that will be on the test."
    "Someone asks whether Monday's exam will be cumulative and receives that one response that knocks the air out of the room."
    "{i}Right... Exams, track, a planning hour that I normally dislike, and whatever else the day has hidden under the floorboards.{/i}"
    "{i}Balanced schedule. Extremely normal. Nothing to see here.{/i}"
    "{i}...Holy hell, I need a chill pill.{/i}"
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "By the time lunch arrives, the next few pages on my notebook are less notes and more random stories and stick drawings based on my favorite games."
    nier "There's this one that's a continuation of a previous piece about a guy who learns to accept his fate in order to escape a Groundhog Day-esque sequence."
    nier "Honestly not my greatest piece, but it certainly exists."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0523_1_5
    scene bg corridor
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3 
    stop music fadeout 1.0
    with wipeleft_scene
    play music schooldays
    "Asahina finds me before I can decide whether to eat alone or rendezvous with Monika or somebody else."
    show asahina neut at t11
    ah "Roof?"
    mc "...No greeting?"
    ah "Hi. Roof?"
    "She says it like the correction cost her actual money."
    mc "Sure."
    "We join the hallway current, then break from it near the stairwell."
    "Asahina walks half a step ahead of me, lunch bag swinging from one hand, phone in the other."
    "She doesn't say much, contrary to her usual behavior, but neither do I."
    "{i}Progress that'll be set back in a week, or hunger. Hard to say.{/i}"
    show asahina at thide
    hide asahina
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    scene bg rooftop
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3 
    with wipeleft_scene
    play sound moddooropen
    "The door opens onto sunlight, wind, and a lunch period already in progress."
    "Tsubaki is sitting near the same shaded wall from Wednesday."
    "Her bento box is open in her lap and a yellow notebook sits beside her, closed but protected by one careful hand like it might escape."
    show tsubaki neut at t22
    show asahina neut at t21
    "She looks up at the both of us. For half a second, she looks pleased."
    "Then her face realizes it has been caught doing that and tries to quietly resign."
    ts "Oh, uh...what's up?"
    ah "Were you already here?"
    mc "No, she teleported here."
    ts "I technically got here first, yes."
    mc "...Technically?"
    ts "I mean...I swear I didn't follow you!"
    ts "I just thought maybe you would come up here again since you did the other day."
    ts "...Retroactively, that sounds worse out loud than it did in my head."
    "She clasps both hands around her container and looks down at it with immediate regret."
    ts "Sorry if that's weird or, uh, anything."
    ah "...Dude, you're allowed to sit on a roof."
    mc "It {i}is{/i} public access, even if semi-forbidden."
    ah "That sounds like something you made up."
    mc "Yeah, that's how naming works."
    ts "So...you're cool with it?"
    ah "Yep. Now scoot over."
    "Tsubaki moves her person, looking almost grateful for a command like she's some sort of golden retriever."
    "The rooftop wind picks at the edge of Asahina's napkin, then gives up when she traps it under her drink."
    "For a little while, lunch proceeds as usual, with nobody and no offhanded topics to intervene."
    "The dichotomy of the two girls' eating styles is something that needs to be studied."
    "Tsubaki eats neatly whereas Asahina eats like she's an office worker with only thirty seconds left of her break."
    "I put the end of a carrot at the edge of my mouth and then suck inwards, almost choking myself in the process."
    ts "So I heard you're back to running?"
    ts "Plantar fasciitis, right? I wouldn't wish that on my worst enemy, it's so annoying."
    ts "Healing well, though?"
    mc "More or less. At least my foot's still attached."
    ah "You're always so vague with your injuries, I swear."
    mc "It covers the important bits, so it works, right?"
    mc "Also, wait, who told you I was injured?"
    ts "Charlie."
    mc "...And who the hell is Charlie?"
    ts "My friend. I thought you two were both distance, no?"
    mc "I guess? I barely even talk to the other guys on the team, let alone know them by name."
    mc "I just show up, do my thing, and go home."
    "Tsubaki shrugs and nods her head as if she's taking her time to either rationalize or relate to my statement."
    ts "...So practice the other day was okay?"
    mc "Yeah. Coach put me on light work, and today is honestly probably more of the same."
    mc "I think the plan is to remind my body that running for more than one or two laps exists."
    ts "So what events do you run?"
    mc "Sixteen hundred and up. Sometimes the gauntlet all in the same meet."
    mc "Which that all means I specialize in making bad decisions slowly."
    ah "Accurate."
    "She says it without teeth. A gentle hit instead of a punch."
    ts "I could never do that."
    ts "Running one lap in gym class already feels like torture."
    mc "I mean, that's still more active than, like, most people...probably."
    "Tsubaki smiles into her food before she can stop herself."
    ah "You were right about the poster, by the way."
    ts "Oh yeah?"
    ah "Yeah, seriously!"
    ah "Some people also said it was really nice. I'm almost blushing from all the hype."
    ts "Oh, uh...I'm glad it worked out, then."
    "Asahina stares up, grinning."
    ah "Not that I was fishing."
    mc "Oh my lord, no one accused you..."
    ah "Okay, but hear me out: shut up."
    "A beat passes before my sister rustles her napkin."
    "Tsubaki watches us for a second with that same delayed smile, seemingly trying to fit in with our banter."
    ts "...I like how you two talk."
    "Her chopsticks stay lifted over her bento for a second."
    "She seems to notice only after the rice starts sliding loose, and she lowers them carefully like she has been caught holding something fragile."
    mc "...And how do we talk?"
    ah "Badly? Goodly?"
    "Tsubaki smiles, but it arrives a little late."
    ts "No, I mean..."
    ts "You don't sound like you're checking every sentence before you're allowed to say it."
    "The wind pulls at the edge of her notebook."
    "She presses one palm over it and keeps her eyes there."
    ts "You just...say things. And then the other person is still there."
    "That comes out too softly to be dramatic."
    "It still makes Asahina put her drink down."
    ah "I mean, he's my brother. He's kind of legally required to be there."
    mc "Also maybe bribed by leftovers without a name."
    "The joke is small enough to give the moment a handle without covering it."
    ts "That sounds nice, honestly."
    "Asahina glances at me, then back at Tsubaki."
    ah "You can talk weird up here too, if you want."
    ts "I'll try to keep the weird at a...responsible volume."
    mc "Completely up to you."
    "Tsubaki's next bite waits untouched while she decides whether that means she has been accepted."
    "By the time she eats it, lunch has started feeling like something with an ending."
    stop music fadeout 1.0
    "That is when the rooftop door opens again."
    "{i}That God-forsaken...{/i}"
    play sound moddooropen
    show asahina neut at t31
    show tsubaki neut at t32
    show matsuda neut at t33
    "Matsuda steps through with one hand lifted near her face and a folded sheet of paper pinched between two gloved fingers."
    "She looks pleased with the entrance before she has checked whether the room she entered is ready for one."
    play music enterm
    ma "Kareda! Consider your mission utterly completed!" # she takes on a chuuni persona in this scene
    ma "Your sentence has been commuted. The faculty archive resisted at first, but mercy prevailed with a little persuasion."
    "All she receives is stares."
    "Tsubaki closes her eyes with the practiced patience of someone who has translated this language before breakfast."
    ts "You got my extension form signed?"
    ma "That is one way to drain all color from the tale, but yes."
    ah "...What extension form?"
    ts "Yeah, so I may have flubbed up. I put a due assignment in the wrong notebook and didn't notice until after it was collected."
    ts "Matsuda was going past the faculty office, so she said she'd ask whether I could turn it in Monday."
    ma "And I returned with official mercy, stamped and witnessed."
    mc "Official mercy, huh? In the form of eye-grating paperwork?"
    ma "Paperwork is the native body of mercy, my dear comrade."
    "She hands the paper to Tsubaki with a flourish that almost gives the wind joint custody."
    "Tsubaki catches it with both hands."
    ts "Thank you."
    ma "Naturally."
    ma "The Azure Eye sees clerical weakness and strikes before it spreads."
    mc "...Azure Eye?"
    ma "A working title."
    "{i}But your eyes are green...{/i}"
    "She says it lightly, but her eyes flick from Tsubaki to Asahina to me, counting the group before the group has agreed to be counted."
    mc "Do we get warning before the title leaves beta?"
    ma "Warnings are for lesser prophecies."
    ah "Is this a, uh, normal Friday thing?"
    ts "Kinda? She has her phases."
    "Matsuda looks at me again."
    "For one second, the performance tightens around her instead of flowing out of her."
    ma "And you, [player]."
    ma "My will of the Azure Eye whispers to me that you have been in exceptionally good spirits, yes?"
    mc "I've been..."
    mc "...Huh?"
    ma "No need to stagger, comrade. Life rarely accepts one concrete proof."
    "I take a sip of my drink in an attempt to escape her clutches of extremely awkward social convention."
    "Matsuda turns back to Tsubaki before the moment can become a conversation."
    ma "My business concludes. I should depart before the bell tolls and shackles my unspoken powers once more."
    "{i}UNSPOKEN?!{/i}"
    ts "Wait, hold on, did you eat?"
    ma "I consumed a rather exquisite melon bread in transit."
    ts "That is not lunch! Did you not pay attention in primary health?!"
    ma "Hark, don't be like that. It had structural integrity, which is sufficient fuel for one such as I."
    "Tsubaki reaches into her lunch bag and pulls out a small wrapped rice cracker."
    "She holds it up without a word."
    "Matsuda looks at it, then at her."
    "When she accepts it, the movement is smaller than the rest of her entrance."
    ma "...Thank ya."
    "The plain words pass quickly."
    "She seems to realize she used them only after they are already out."
    ts "Eat real food later, please."
    ma "I will negotiate with dinner."
    ma "Until the next eclipse, then."
    mc "There isn't an eclipse today..."
    ma "Then the next lunch period, i.e. tomorrow, will have to suffice. Now ta-ta!"
    show matsuda at thide
    hide matsuda
    stop music fadeout 1.0
    play sound moddoorclose
    "She disappears through the door with the rice cracker tucked carefully in her hand."
    "The roof feels a little larger after she leaves, like the air needs time to settle back into place."
    show asahina neut at t21
    show tsubaki neut at t22
    "Asahina looks at the door, then at Tsubaki."
    mc "...So how stressed was she there?"
    "My sister puzzledly points at the roof door."
    play music dailyfantasy
    ah "Wait, she knew you were up here?"
    "Tsubaki presses her lips together."
    ts "She probably guessed."
    ts "Or she saw me come up. Or she asked someone."
    ts "...I don't know which answer sounds least weird."
    "That last part comes out quieter."
    mc "Does she do that a lot?"
    ts "Not in a bad way."
    ts "She just...gets attached to patterns, kinda."
    ts "People, too, sometimes."
    "Asahina's mouth opens like she has a joke ready but ultimately lets it go."
    ah "You don't have to apologize for her."
    ts "Sorry."
    "Asahina gives me a look."
    "I give her the smallest possible shrug."
    ah "Okay, new rule: You're still allowed on the roof, and that apology just now? That doesn't count."
    "Tsubaki looks relieved enough that the sentence seems heavier than Asahina meant it to be."
    "Then the warning bell rings below us, thin and distant."
    mc "We should go before the staircase turns into a traffic jam."
    ah "Practical. Suspicious."
    ts "Maybe the roof has phases too."
    mc "Oh my lord..."
    "Asahina laughs, not because the line is sharp, but because Tsubaki actually offered it."
    "The three of us pack up without turning that into anything bigger."
    show asahina at thide
    hide asahina
    show tsubaki at thide
    hide tsubaki
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "Afternoon classes take the moment away, as afternoon classes often do."
    nier "By the time the final bell rings, every subject has reminded us that Monday is approaching with paperwork."
    nier "I change for practice with the mild dread of someone who knows his body is about to discover how much a week can take from a stride."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0523_2
    scene bg track_day
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_afternoon zorder 3 
    stop music fadeout 1.0
    with wipeleft_scene
    play music daily
    "The track has held onto the afternoon sun."
    "It comes back through the soles of my shoes while I cross the infield, warm enough to make the whole place feel awake."
    "A few sprinters work on starts near the straightaway."
    "The distance group has gathered by the infield, talking in that loose, tired way runners talk before choosing to become miserable on purpose."
    "{i}There they are. My people, unfortunately.{/i}"
    show track_coach neut at t11
    track_coach "[player]."
    "Coach does not shout this time."
    "He is already near the lane line with his clipboard tucked against one hip."
    "The look he gives me starts at my shoes and works its way up like he is checking whether I arrived assembled correctly."
    track_coach "Foot?"
    mc "Quiet."
    track_coach "Good. We keep it that way."
    track_coach "Twenty minutes easy on the outside. You need to work on stamina, so again, I want rhythm, not proof."
    track_coach "After that, four relaxed strides if the foot doesn't yell."
    mc "Twenty easy, then four relaxed strides."
    track_coach "Easy. No more, no less."
    "He repeats the word because he knows exactly where I tend to hide the stupid decisions."
    mc "Roger wilco..."
    track_coach "I know. I just want your legs to hear it."
    show track_coach at thide
    hide track_coach
    "I join the outside lane and let the first hundred meters be ugly."
    "There is no point pretending the body comes back online all at once."
    "My foot stays quiet. My calves complain in smaller print. My lungs wake up, annoyed but functional."
    "The pace is slow enough to bruise my pride, which is probably why Coach assigned it."
    "By the second lap, the movement starts to remember itself."
    "Distance running is where I am supposed to settle."
    "Not the violent argument of a sprint start, not the twelve-second dare of turning the body into a weapon."
    "This is time, posture, breath, and the patience to let easy become honest."
    "That is the version I like telling myself."
    "The real version is that my shoulders creep up by lap three and my left foot starts landing too far ahead, like the rest of me is trying to get to the future before I do."
    show track_coach neut at t11
    track_coach "Arms!"
    "Coach's voice reaches me from the infield."
    "I drop my shoulders."
    track_coach "Shorter step! You're reaching!"
    "I shorten the stride."
    "The change helps immediately, which is annoying in the specific way good advice always is."
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "Twenty minutes becomes a loop of small corrections."
    nier "Relax the hands. Stop reaching. Land under the hip. Let the pace stay boring. Breathe like continuing is the plan."
    nier "Command after command after command, and the body tries to follow them all at once, which is how it ends up doing none of them well."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0523_3
    scene bg track_day
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_evening zorder 3 
    with wipeleft_scene
    "By the cooldown, sweat has collected at my collar and the afternoon has started leaning toward evening."
    "My foot is still quiet, fortunately."
    "The rest of me is tired in places that have not had opinions for a week. My lower back feels slightly blown out."
    show track_coach neut at t11
    track_coach "Better after the third lap, but a bit less controlled near the end."
    mc "I'll take better for now."
    track_coach "We can push past that threshold, though."
    track_coach "Fitness is still there, but you're still a bit rusty."
    track_coach "Your shoulders creep when you get impatient, and you overstride when you think about pace instead of feel."
    mc "So...yet again, it's mental, right?"
    track_coach "Your brain is useful when it stays in its lane, much like what your form should be doing."
    "A nearby teammate--probably Charlie--coughs into his fist."
    "I choose to interpret it as seasonal allergies and not betrayal."
    track_coach "Stretch, hydrate, and get out of here."
    track_coach "Do not turn tonight or tomorrow night into extra training because you feel behind."
    track_coach "We got an invitational soon. Can't have you becoming the team cripple."
    "That cuts closer to the bone than the form notes."
    mc "...Got it."
    track_coach "Good."
    track_coach "Once exams are done, we reassess."
    track_coach "Academic stress makes athletes stupid in creative ways, and I would like you to avoid contributing to the data."
    mc "I'll do my best to protect the sample."
    track_coach "Hydrate, hydrate, hydrate. I cannot stress that enough. Hotter weather means more water."
    track_coach "Now take it easy. You know your weekend mileage, don't be a hero."
    show track_coach at thide
    hide track_coach
    "He walks off, leaving the instruction behind."
    "I drink water, stretch until my hamstrings stop tightening every time I move, and decide not to prove anything else today."
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "Practice ends clean."
    nier "I pass by the club room on the way out to see if anybody is there, but the lights are already off with no bags in sight."
    nier "On the way home, I pick up a newspaper for my mom since I know she likes to catch up on things over the weekend."
    nier "Why she doesn't use her phone for that is a mystery, but I don't ask."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0523_4
    scene bg kitchen
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_evening zorder 3 
    stop music fadeout 1.0
    with wipeleft_scene
    play music dailyleisure
    "Home smells like clean laundry and dinner that has already happened."
    "A covered plate waits on the counter with my name on a sticky note."
    "A second note is stuck to the top."
    # Future note: make an actual sticky note image and use that to show the notes instead of just writing them in dialogue. That way they can be more visually distinct and less likely to be confused with narration.
    "{i}Eat first. Shower second. Laptop third. - Mom{/i}"
    "The order is too specific to argue with."
    "I eat standing at the counter for the first two bites, then remember I am technically civilized and sit down."
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "Dinner is taken care of and cleaned up without turning into an event."
    nier "I shower until track stops living on my skin, change into house clothes, and sit on the edge of my bed with the laptop closed beside me."
    nier "It is the same laptop I use for homework, club drafts, game notes, and several searches I would deny under oath."
    nier "Tonight, somehow, it looks like a door handle in the most bizarre way."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0523_5
    scene bg living_room_night
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_home zorder 3 
    stop music fadeout 1.0
    with wipeleft_scene
    play music fantasyserenity
    "Mom is in the living room when I come downstairs."
    "The coffee table has been cleared except for her tablet, a notebook, two pens, and a rather vocal empty space that says 'please have a discussion around me.'"
    "Asahina is nowhere in sight."
    "Her door upstairs is closed, which probably means homework, texting Sam, homework with Sam, or pretending those are all separate activities."
    show mom neut at t11
    "Mom looks up when I stop near the couch."
    mom "Hey, you survived!"
    mc "Foot's fine. Coach says my mechanics are rusty, but what else is new."
    mom "One day at a time, though, right?"
    mc "Yeah, pretty much. That's all I {i}can{/i} do."
    "I sit and set my laptop on the coffee table."
    "For a second, neither of us opens it."
    mom "Before we open that, ground rules."
    "Her voice moves into the practical register she uses for contracts, furniture instructions, and any situation where panic would be inefficient."
    mc "Okay."
    mom "We are looking at an option."
    mom "Not making a verdict, not committing your life, not picking the name that goes on every future holiday conversation cause God knows neither of us need that."
    mom "I meant it when I said you could come to me when you were ready."
    mom "I also know deadlines don't wait for a perfect mood, and next week is mostly going to be midterms eating everyone inside."
    "It is less dramatic than I expected, which makes it harder to push away."
    mom "So tonight, we look."
    mom "We write down questions, think of any other routes we want to explore."
    mom "We close the laptop before we get psyched out by tuition rates and a whole bunch of other numbers."
    mc "Numbers always have their way..."
    mom "That's why this is just recon."
    "I open the laptop."
    "The blank search bar waits with more confidence than either of us."
    mc "Yeah..."
    mc "It's just weird."
    mc "When I said I wanted to see the world, it sounded normal."
    mc "Like one of those things people say because the future is too far away to argue."
    mc "Then you found a real place with buildings and deadlines and a page that probably says welcome in a clean font."
    mc "Now it feels like I said something too loudly and the world started taking notes."
    mom "That sounds like consequences, yes."
    "She writes the date at the top of the notebook, then underlines it once -- just enough to make me realize this is really something I have to worry about."
    mom "To reiterate, you are graduating in less than a year."
    mom "Applications do not care whether you feel ready."
    mom "Entrance exams do not care whether track is in your schedule."
    mom "Deadlines do not care whether the house has had a long or busy week."
    mom "Now I wish they did..."
    "She exhales through her nose."
    mom "But they don't."
    mc "Mhm..."
    "The laptop fan starts its tiny unnecessary whisper."
    mc "I know I have to think about it."
    mc "I just hate that thinking about it makes everything feel unstable."
    mom "What part?"
    mc "All of it."
    mc "If I pick somewhere far away, then I'm far away, simple as."
    mc "If I pick somewhere close, then I wonder whether I was only brave while it was hypothetical."
    mc "If I pick wrong, I have to live inside a mistake I made because a website looked professional enough to convince me."
    mom "Let me stop you right there."
    mom "You're not choosing a final version of yourself."
    mc "It feels like I am, mom."
    mom "I know."
    mom "But you are choosing a next environment. That matters. Trust me, it matters a lot."
    mom "It is not the same as a life sentence."
    "A small laugh gets out before I can stop it."
    mc "Lawyer mom says not a life sentence. Add one sin to the counter."
    mom "Lawyer mom is very careful with sentence length."
    "That helps enough to let the next part of the conversation out."
    mom "Can I ask something before you build a defense around the answer?"
    mc "Depends how attorney-like it is."
    mom "Eight out of ten."
    mc "Then no promises."
    mom "When you imagine leaving, what do you feel first?"
    "I look at her."
